      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s an integer type whose access is guaranteed to be atomic even in the face of signal interrupts.  AFAIK it\u0027s never wrapped with special instructions, rather it\u0027s a type that can be written to or read from (not both of course) in a single instruction (based on the target architecture).\n\nAFAIK no other type in C or C++ has the same guarantee.\n\nOn its own sig_atomic_t is just an integer type, there is nothing else special about it, so volatile is also needed to prevent the compiler from optimizing away repeated reads of it.",
